From 98c81f0239bebfbb98eea57b694d244abd2f4b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skynizz <182822215+Skynizz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:50:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Accumulated reference (mode 3), per-channel directions in KRC, debug cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Mode 3: sum of each frame's spherical harmonics per pixel, displayed as a mean,
  reset on every lamp change. The old reference averaged images that were already
  clamped: noisy, it lost energy in bright areas (KRC looked +56 % there).
- KRC: directional moments per channel (mean of colour x direction), linear, relit
  with the mean; a short direction is a measurement, no more fallback to the normal.
- Barrier before the cache passes.

